title: No way to skip the image build for a local dzil install
updated: 2026-08-25T13:46:36Z
---

after_build builds unconditionally (documented), but mid-release-cycle the Dockerfile's cpanm --installdeps resolves from CPAN and must fail while the dep chain is unreleased (karr pins Git::Native 0.006 etc.). That makes dzil install/test/build of the consumer impossible locally until everything ships. Precheck has DZIL_DOCKER_API_SKIP_PRECHECK; the build itself has no escape hatch. Consider DZIL_DOCKER_API_SKIP=1 skipping before_build+after_build with a loud log line.

Committed with DZIL_DOCKER_API_SKIP; release refuses with the variable set.
